{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"06f56a5a-0464-4142-a1d9-c67d7bb41c16","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A line of symmetry divides this regular hexagon into two matching halves. Folding along that line would make the halves overlap exactly.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Regular hexagon: symmetry"},{"op":"diagram","id":"hexagon","region":"right","primitives":[{"kind":"line","points":[[0.5,0.16],[0.818,0.33],[0.818,0.67],[0.5,0.84],[0.182,0.67],[0.182,0.33],[0.5,0.16]],"stroke":"solid","meaning":"regular hexagon outline"}]},{"op":"text","id":"fold","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Fold line → matching halves"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"06f56a5a-0464-4142-a1d9-c67d7bb41c16","step":{"id":"s2","script":"First, join opposite vertices. Each dashed line is a fold line. There are three lines of symmetry of this type.","ops":[{"op":"line","id":"vertex1","canvas_id":"hexagon","from":[0.5,0.16],"to":[0.5,0.84],"stroke":"dashed","meaning":"symmetry axis through opposite vertices"},{"op":"line","id":"vertex2","canvas_id":"hexagon","from":[0.182,0.33],"to":[0.818,0.67],"stroke":"dashed","meaning":"symmetry axis through opposite vertices"},{"op":"line","id":"vertex3","canvas_id":"hexagon","from":[0.182,0.67],"to":[0.818,0.33],"stroke":"dashed","meaning":"symmetry axis through opposite vertices"},{"op":"text","id":"vertexcount","anchor":{"el":"fold","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"3 through opposite vertices"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Are there fold lines that do not pass through vertices?","expected_gist":"Yes: lines through the midpoints of opposite sides."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"06f56a5a-0464-4142-a1d9-c67d7bb41c16","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Three more lines join midpoints of opposite sides. Together, these give six lines of symmetry—not the sides themselves.","ops":[{"op":"line","id":"midpoint1","canvas_id":"hexagon","from":[0.182,0.5],"to":[0.818,0.5],"stroke":"dashed","meaning":"symmetry axis through opposite side midpoints"},{"op":"line","id":"midpoint2","canvas_id":"hexagon","from":[0.341,0.245],"to":[0.659,0.755],"stroke":"dashed","meaning":"symmetry axis through opposite side midpoints"},{"op":"line","id":"midpoint3","canvas_id":"hexagon","from":[0.659,0.245],"to":[0.341,0.755],"stroke":"dashed","meaning":"symmetry axis through opposite side midpoints"},{"op":"text","id":"total","anchor":{"el":"vertexcount","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"+ 3 through side midpoints = 6"}],"checkpoint":null}}
